  "reason": "Evidence: config_043 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) is the best result so far (acc=0.635, F1=0.618), and config_003 shows RNA-only with pca_n2000 is notably weaker (acc=0.591), confirming multimodal fusion adds value. However, all three completed experiments use pca_n2000 for RNA, leaving the RNA encoder choice entirely untested. Question: Does a learned RNA representation (scgpt) outperform linear PCA (pca_n2000) when paired with the same image encoder, aggregation, and fusion? config_049 changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scgpt while holding imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, and weighted fusion constant, directly isolating the encoder effect. This is the highest-value next experiment because the RNA representation is a fundamental design axis with large uncertainty; if scgpt substantially improves over PCA, it redirects the search toward learned representations, whereas a null result confirms PCA sufficiency and shifts focus to aggregation or image-encoder choices."
}

